<section class="g-paper" id="them">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="tick">\</span> 03 · The other side</div>
    <h2>We check the team before you meet them.</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      Job boards ask you to prove yourself to a company that has proved nothing to you. A request reaches you only after
      the team clears its own checks.
    </p>
    <div class="chk">
      <div class="chk-top">
        <span class="pf-k"><span class="pf-dot"></span> Example team · consumer internet</span><span class="chk-tag"
          >Platform team · reports to VP Engineering</span
        >
      </div>
      <div class="chk-row">
        <span>Is the headcount real?</span><em>Approved and funded, or we don't list it.</em><b class="pill pill--ink"
          >Verified</b
        >
      </div>
      <div class="chk-row">
        <span>How many rounds?</span><em>Stated up front. If it changes, you hear it from us.</em><b class="pill"
          >Three</b
        >
      </div>
      <div class="chk-row">
        <span>How fast do they decide?</span><em>Measured from your final interview.</em><b class="pill">6 days</b>
      </div>
      <div class="chk-row">
        <span>How long has the manager been there?</span><em>The person you would report to.</em><b class="pill"
          >4 yrs</b
        >
      </div>
      <div class="chk-row">
        <span>Do people stay?</span><em>Retention on their recent hires through us.</em><b class="pill pill--flag"
          >One flag</b
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-checks outc">
      <div><h3>Cleared</h3><p>The request reaches you with the role, the team and what they weighted.</p></div>
      <div>
        <h3>Flagged</h3><p>It reaches you with the flag and the reason written out. You decide whether it matters.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Declined</h3><p>It doesn't reach you. Unfunded headcount, or a role that has churned twice this year.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
